<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuanian 91-day T-bill rate dips further.</title>
<headline>Lithuanian 91-day T-bill rate dips further.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield at an auction of Lithuanian 91-day Treasury bills dipped to 10.58 percent, compared with an auction last week of 98-day paper, when the average yield was 11.38 percent, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY  AV YIELD   (LAST TIME)  MIN/MAX    ISSUE  BID    SOLD</p>
<p> 91-day     10.58	 11.38    8.90/11.25    50  106.278   50</p>
<p>Settlement date for today's auction was November 28 and the bills mature on February 27.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
